  "summary": "Overnight markets leaned risk-off: U.S. Treasury yields fell about 23\u201327bp across the 2Y\u201310Y over five days on safe-haven demand, even as Fed minutes and Governor Waller kept a hawkish rate path in view. Equities were under pressure with the S&P 500 near 7176 and the VIX at 28.44; gold held near $3,515 after its worst week since March. Crude stayed elevated (WTI $83.98, Brent $92.57) on Hormuz uncertainty, IEA warnings that pre-war normality looks unreachable, and tanker incidents as a third U.S. carrier arrived. The dollar stayed firm in spots dated Nov 20\u2014USD/JPY 158.64, EUR/USD 1.099, AUD and NZD weaker on the month\u2014while policy rhetoric diverged: ECB officials flagged rising inflation pressure, Japan\u2019s core CPI hit a year-high with Ueda open to hikes, and the RBNZ stressed inflation still above the 2% midpoint.",
